	Section:
		Text: Frame and overlays
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Frame
		Paragraph: A `Frame` is laid out in its place, like a `Block`, and then shifted by `Offset` (top, right, bottom, left). Its space stays where it was and the boxes after it do not move. One side of each pair stays `auto`.
			Style: intro
		Text: No Offset
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Box:
				Width: 200
			Text: In its place in the flow
				Style: card
		Paragraph: The paragraph after the Frame.
			Box:
				Margin: 6 0 16 0
		Text: Offset: 12 auto auto 40  (12 down, 40 to the right)
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Offset: 12 auto auto 40
			Box:
				Width: 200
			Text: Shifted down and to the right
				Style: card
		Paragraph: The paragraph after the Frame does not move: the shifted box covers it.
			Box:
				Margin: 6 0 16 0
		Text: Offset: auto 0 0 auto  (no shift) and Offset: -10 auto auto 0  (10 up)
			Style: label
		Frame:
			Offset: auto 0 0 auto
			Box:
